    "body": "`MIP_WARL` is marked `impl-def-behavior: true` and categorized as `WARL`, but unlike other impl-def rules in this file it is missing `kind` and `instance` (e.g., `kind: extension`, `instance: Sm`). This likely breaks schema validation / rule classification; add the missing fields to match the existing pattern for WARL rules (see `MISA_WARL`, `MEDELEG_WARL`, etc.).\n```suggestion\n    impl-def-behavior: true\n    kind: extension\n    instance: Sm\n    impl-def-category: WARL\n  - name: mie_enc\n    tags: [\"norm:mip_mie_enc_txt\", \"norm:mie_enc_img\"]\n  - name: MIE_WARL\n    tag: \"norm:mie_enc_img\"\n    impl-def-behavior: true\n    kind: extension\n    instance: Sm\n```",
